            "review_title": "Review at An Cua Saigon",
            "review_text": "Travel38809428432\n1 contribution\n0\nCome to eat.\nApr 2026 • Couples\nIt happened to see a restaurant on IG and come to try and it was a pretty impressive experience.\nThe first impression is that the space is small but cosy, a bit “hidden” so the feeling is also interesting. The evening is quite crowded, so if you go to a group, you should book a table first. Friendly staff, pleasant talk.\nAs far as food is concerned, it is very fresh. I call salty egg fever with extra seafood sauce, and some other dishes, such as pancakes or silk sauce sauce, taste quite thick, easy to eat, and suits many people. Sure meat, not damaged. However, the fever is mild western.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten April 11, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
